---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TrustStrip from '../../components/TrustStrip.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I charge two EVs on a 200-amp panel?",
    "answer": "Yes, with smart load sharing. Two chargers share a single 60A circuit. When one car charges alone, it gets 48A. When both plug in, each gets 24A. Both cars are typically full by morning."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is dynamic load balancing?",
    "answer": "Dynamic load balancing uses current transformers on your main service lines to monitor total home electricity usage in real time. The system automatically adjusts EV charging amperage to prevent exceeding your panel capacity."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do both chargers need to be the same brand?",
    "answer": "For power-sharing features, yes, most systems require matched pairs (e.g., two Tesla Wall Connectors or two Wallbox units). For independent circuits with dynamic load management, different brands can be used."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will charging be slower with two cars?",
    "answer": "When both cars are actively charging, each receives reduced power. However, since most vehicles sit plugged in for 8-10 hours overnight, even at reduced rates both cars reach full charge before morning."
  },
  {
    "question": "What if I add a third EV later?",
    "answer": "Systems like the Tesla Wall Connector support up to six units on a single shared circuit. We design installations with future expandability in mind, provisioning panel capacity and conduit for additional stations."
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Multi-EV Home Charging Solutions in Issaquah | Dual Charger Install"
  description="Multi-EV home charging installations in Issaquah WA. Smart dual-charger load sharing for two electric vehicles on one electrical service. Call (425) 380-0019."
  canonicalPath="/services/multi-ev-home-charging/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services/' },
    { name: 'Multi-EV Home Charging' }
  ]} />

  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 840px;">
        <span class="section-tag" style="background: rgba(132, 204, 22, 0.2); color: #84cc16;">Specialized EV Service</span>
        <h1>Multi-EV Home Charging & Dual Charger Installation in Issaquah</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">Two electric vehicles, one residential panel. Our electricians install intelligent load-sharing charging systems that allow both cars to charge overnight without exceeding your service capacity or tripping your main breaker.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta-wrap">
          <a href="tel:+14253800019" class="btn btn-lime"><span>📞</span><span>Call (425) 380-0019</span></a>
          <a href="/locations/" class="btn btn-outline-white">View All 15 Service Areas</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <TrustStrip />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="rich-content" style="max-width: 900px; margin-inline: auto;">
        <h2>What This Service Covers</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Dual Level 2 charging station installation with smart load balancing</li>
          <li>Power-sharing configuration (Tesla dual Wall Connector, Wallbox Pulsar Plus pairs)</li>
          <li>NEC Article 220 multi-vehicle load calculations</li>
          <li>Panel capacity assessment for simultaneous 48A draws</li>
          <li>Subpanel additions for dedicated dual-EV charging circuits</li>
          <li>Wi-Fi and low-voltage data cable installation for charger communication</li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/multi-ev-home-dual-charging.jpg" 
            alt="Dual electric vehicle home charging system installed in 2-car Issaquah WA garage 98029"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Smart dual-charger installation featuring automated dynamic power sharing on a single electrical service.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <h2>Technical Background & How It Works</h2>
        <p>Two-EV households are increasingly common across Issaquah. When both vehicles plug in after work, they can demand 96 continuous amps combined. On a standard 200-amp service, that leaves only 104 amps for the rest of the home, a margin too thin for comfort.</p>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/panel-upgrade-200-amp-circuit-breakers.jpg" 
            alt="Service panel load management module for two EV chargers in Issaquah estate home"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Intelligent energy management modules throttle charging during peak household appliance usage.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <p>Smart load-sharing chargers solve this by dividing available circuit capacity dynamically. When both cars are plugged in, each receives half the current. As one battery fills up, the other automatically ramps to full speed. Both vehicles are charged by morning, and the panel never exceeds its rated capacity.</p>

        <p>This service is available throughout all 15 Issaquah neighborhoods, including <a href="/locations/issaquah-highlands/">Issaquah Highlands</a>, <a href="/locations/talus/">Talus</a>, <a href="/locations/klahanie/">Klahanie</a>, and <a href="/locations/olde-town-issaquah/">Olde Town Issaquah</a>. Browse our full <a href="/locations/">locations hub</a> to find your area.</p>

        <h2>When to Contact Us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your household has two or more electric vehicles</li>
          <li>You need both EVs charged every night but lack panel capacity for two independent 60A circuits</li>
          <li>You want Tesla power-sharing or Wallbox Power Boost installed</li>
          <li>Your main breaker trips when both cars charge simultaneously</li>
          <li>You are adding a second EV and need charging infrastructure for it</li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/modern-issaquah-garage-ev-charger.jpg" 
            alt="Dual wall-mounted EV charging units configured for balanced overnight charging"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Clean, symmetrical dual-station layout keeping charging cables organized and off garage floors.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <p>For technical questions about multi-ev home charging in Issaquah, call our dispatch line directly at <a href="tel:+14253800019">(425) 380-0019</a>. Licensed under <a href="https://apps.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=296-46B" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WAC 296-46B</a> and fully compliant with NEC Article 625 standards.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQAccordion items={faqs} />

  <section class="section" style="background: #ffffff; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title-wrap">
        <span class="section-tag">Related Solutions</span>
        <h2>Related EV Charging Services</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="card-title">Level 2 EV Charger Installation</h3>
